<!-- ==================== SHEET 5 — ABSTRACT ==================== -->
<p class="ft">Abstract</p>
<p>Modern software development is fragmented across a large number of disconnected tools. A student
or an early-career developer typically moves between a conversational assistant for general
questions, a separate service to query private documents, another to review code, an online
compiler to run it, a competitive-programming judge to practise on, and yet another generator to
scaffold new projects. Each of these tools maintains its own account, its own interface conventions
and its own copy of the user's data, and none of them shares context with the others. The cost of
this fragmentation is paid in context switching, in duplicated effort, and in a loss of privacy
whenever private material is uploaded to an unrelated third-party service.</p>
<p><b>DevAssist AI</b> is a unified, web-based developer assistance platform that consolidates seven
such capabilities behind a single authenticated account and a single design system. The platform
provides: <i>Global AI</i>, a general-purpose streaming chat assistant with persistent, searchable
history; <i>Secret AI</i>, a private document question-answering module in which answers are
grounded strictly in documents the user has uploaded; <i>Code Analyzer</i>, which returns structured
defect reports, an optimised rewrite and a time-complexity comparison; <i>Online Compiler</i>, a
zero-setup multi-language execution environment; <i>VoidMain</i>, a competitive-programming judge
with problem set, verdicts and leaderboard; <i>Ignite</i>, an AI project builder that generates a
complete multi-file frontend project from a single natural-language prompt; and <i>Circuit</i>,
which converts a question into a validated, animatable step-by-step visual explanation.</p>
<p>The system is implemented as three independently deployed services: a framework-free
HTML/CSS/JavaScript frontend, a Spring Boot 3 backend written in Java following a layered clean
architecture, and a Python FastAPI inference engine. Persistence and authentication are provided by
a managed PostgreSQL instance, with every stored row keyed to the owning user's universally unique
identifier so that multi-tenant isolation is enforced uniformly across all seven modules.
Large-language-model access is routed through a provider-abstraction registry that allows the active
vendor and model to be changed by editing a single environment variable, with no code change and no
redeployment of application logic.</p>
<p>A distinguishing engineering constraint of this work is that the entire platform runs on
free-tier infrastructure. Meeting that constraint required a set of deliberate mitigations that are
documented and evaluated in this report: a scheduled keep-alive service that suppresses cold starts,
lazy importing of heavy machine-learning dependencies, per-user sliding-window rate limiting, a
daily token-accounting ledger, sequential generation with exponential backoff, and a
context-injection strategy for document grounding that avoids loading embedding models into a
memory-constrained container. Phase I delivers a fully functional deployed system covering all seven
modules; Phase II will address persistent vector storage, backend code generation and formal
quantitative benchmarking.</p>
<p><b>Keywords:</b> Large Language Models, Retrieval-Augmented Generation, Developer Tools,
Microservices, Multi-Tenant Isolation, Cloud Computing, Automated Code Analysis.</p>

<br clear="all" class="pgbreak">

